{"ts": "2025-12-26T15:24:58.261962Z", "level": "INFO", "event": "TASK.TRADE.PROCESSING", "event_code": "TASK.TRADE.PROCESSING", "trace_id": "TRC-20251226152458-3e0cb4cbf877", "service": "voidpoly", "msg": "处理TRADE阶段任务", "extra": {"task_id": 945, "metadata": {"market": {"id": "1004654", "question": "Trump announces new drug boat strike by December 31?", "slug": "trump-announces-new-drug-boat-strike-by-december-31-848", "outcomes": "[\"Yes\", \"No\"]", "outcome_prices": "[\"0.6\", \"0.4\"]", "active": true, "volume": "7449.858951", "liquidity": "2556.36", "end_date": "2025-12-31T00:00:00Z", "tau": 4, "tags": [], "marks": [], "negRisk": false, "clobTokenIds": "[\"6964852083189420291419638160131379552879469184299038671139171667819333129637\", \"41556087485945391327747081167392745853883364135497696948588244484353157792020\"]"}, "analysis": {"p": 0.68, "n": 0.28, "a": 0.82, "reasons_y": ["Since early September 2025, the US has run a sustained campaign of air and missile strikes on alleged drug boats in the Caribbean and Eastern Pacific, with around 29 reported strikes and at least 105 fatalities as of the Dec. 23 announcement, indicating a high and ongoing operational tempo.citeturn1news49turn1search16turn1search23", "Trump’s January 20, 2025 executive order and subsequent State Department action officially designated multiple Latin American cartels as foreign terrorist organizations and narco-terrorist threats, providing a legal and political framework that supports continued military strikes on vessels associated with these groups.citeturn2search10turn2search2turn0search31", "Trump’s political brand and rhetoric emphasize aggressive, highly publicized use of force against perceived enemies; he has personally announced prior drug-boat strikes on social media and in public events, and messaging repeatedly uses terms like narco-terrorists to justify lethal action.citeturn1search9turn1search13turn2search20", "US Southern Command, the Pentagon, and related outlets have repeatedly released videos and detailed statements about boat strikes under Operation Southern Spear, portraying them as successful precision strikes, which suggests institutional incentives to continue and to publicly acknowledge any new qualifying strike.citeturn0search6turn2search19turn1search8", "The broader Venezuela pressure campaign (sanctions, naval and Coast Guard actions, tanker seizures, and a de facto blockade) is intensifying in late December and framed around cutting off narco-terrorist funding, making another dramatic maritime strike announcement a plausible tool to reinforce coercive leverage before year-end.citeturn1news51turn2news50turn2news52", "The market is already pricing Yes around the low-to-mid 60% range, which implies that informed participants see a substantial chance that at least one additional qualifying strike or previously unannounced strike will be publicly acknowledged within the remaining days of the window."], "reasons_n": ["The remaining time window is short (only a few days until the Dec. 31 deadline), and a new strike on a suspected drug boat was just carried out and announced around Dec. 22–23, increasing the likelihood of a brief operational or communications lull after a fresh, high-profile strike.citeturn1search4turn1search23turn1search8", "Domestic and international criticism over the legality and civilian impact of the maritime strikes is mounting; human-rights organizations and legal analysts have described some of the boat killings as possible extrajudicial executions, raising the political cost of each additional strike and especially of publicly celebrating new ones.citeturn0search23turn2search22turn2search26", "Congress, media, and legal experts are questioning the authority for treating drug trafficking as armed conflict, and recent coverage highlights evidentiary gaps and legal concerns about the militarized drug war at sea, which could encourage the administration and Pentagon to slow or more tightly control further visible strikes in the near term.citeturn0search25turn2search19turn0search8", "The administration has multiple alternative ways to project toughness on narco-terrorism and security in late December, including oil-tanker seizures and blockades, new sanctions and terror-related indictments of cartel leaders, and high-visibility strikes against ISIS targets in Nigeria, any of which can serve the messaging goal without incurring the same legal controversy as another boat strike.citeturn1news51turn2news9turn1news48turn2search10", "Escalating diplomatic tensions with Venezuela and concern from major powers such as Russia and China over US maritime actions and sanctions increase the strategic risk of further lethal strikes on vessels, potentially incentivizing a temporary pause or more cautious approach during an already fraught period.citeturn2news50turn2news52turn1news52", "Some future counternarcotics operations may rely more on Coast Guard interdictions and lower-profile seizures rather than clearly acknowledged missile or air strikes, and any classified or deniable actions against suspected drug boats may not be officially confirmed within the market’s resolution window, resulting in a No even if kinetic activity continues.citeturn1news51turn1search14"]}, "source_analysis_task_id": 943, "marks": ["normal_tau", "trump", "auto_mark"]}, "result": {"allocation": {"cost": 0.034, "dollars": 1, "fraction_of_gross": 0.005797101449275363, "score": 0.005797101449275363, "shares": 17.050298380221655, "side": "YES"}, "decision": "trade", "locked_value": 0, "wealth": 30}}}
